    {
      "id": "5gWkVQ6T1IyT9sehtSHxi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 330.35215523596236,
      "y": 843.368408604921,
      "width": 518.339599609375,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1R",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 453746824,
      "version": 514,
      "versionNonce": 1268518280,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782191170498,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Service generate metrics datapoint and\nsend them to platform\n2. platform ingest, validate and store\nmetrics (normalize metrics) as time series data\n3. User query stored metrics through dashboard,\nfiltering, aggregate across time\n4. Alert rules periodically evaluate against\nstored metrics\n5. when alert condition is breached, then notification\nsent to configured channel (eg: email, slack)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Service generate metrics datapoint and\nsend them to platform\n2. platform ingest, validate and store\nmetrics (normalize metrics) as time series data\n3. User query stored metrics through dashboard,\nfiltering, aggregate across time\n4. Alert rules periodically evaluate against\nstored metrics\n5. when alert condition is breached, then notification\nsent to configured channel (eg: email, slack)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "FoZrUlHuwl1gmZx-2tyiA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 350.53425850155054,
      "y": 1138.0262467390614,
      "width": 77.87997436523438,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1S",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 755604104,
      "version": 12,
      "versionNonce": 1577074568,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782191185299,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*** API\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*** API\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "-Qy2wPtA9PwkxQ67GkdBZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 338.29108685228397,
      "y": 1165.851636851031,
      "width": 652.6128177344341,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1T",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2082988024,
      "version": 205,
      "versionNonce": 806427640,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782191617505,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "// ingest metrics\nPOST /metrics/ingest\n{\n  \"metrics\": [\n    { \"name\": \"cpu_usage\", \"labels\": {\"host\": \"server-1\"}, \"value\": 0.75,\n\"timestamp\": 1640000000 },\n    ...\n  ]\n}\n// query metrics\nGET /metrics/query?query=avg(cpu_usage{region=\"us-\neast\"})&start=A&end=B&step=60 -> { \"timestamps\": [...], \"values\":\n[...] }\n// create alert\nPOST /alerts/rules\n{\n  \"name\": \"High CPU Alert\",\n  \"query\": \"avg(cpu_usage{region='us-east'}) > 0.9\",\n  \"for\": \"5m\",\n  \"notifications\": [\"slack:#oncall\", \"pagerduty:team-infra\"]\n}\n\n// use prototuf and use seralialize data. ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "// ingest metrics\nPOST /metrics/ingest\n{\n  \"metrics\": [\n    { \"name\": \"cpu_usage\", \"labels\": {\"host\": \"server-1\"}, \"value\": 0.75, \"timestamp\": 1640000000 },\n    ...\n  ]\n}\n// query metrics\nGET /metrics/query?query=avg(cpu_usage{region=\"us-east\"})&start=A&end=B&step=60 -> { \"timestamps\": [...], \"values\": [...] }\n// create alert\nPOST /alerts/rules\n{\n  \"name\": \"High CPU Alert\",\n  \"query\": \"avg(cpu_usage{region='us-east'}) > 0.9\",\n  \"for\": \"5m\",\n  \"notifications\": [\"slack:#oncall\", \"pagerduty:team-infra\"]\n}\n\n// use prototuf and use seralialize data. ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "4lsgmkFgIGcNvEulkwBN5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1284.7431557385933,
      "y": -133.28714430541123,
      "width": 824.9793090820312,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1V",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 530079368,
      "version": 535,
      "versionNonce": 1707293944,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782192086860,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*** High level design\n\n\n-- the most naive approach is having servers POST metrics directly to ingestion \nservice, the service do data validate and write it to store\n-- This could quickly overwhelm the service (eg: handle 5M metrics/sec)\n-- to scale this, we will introduce usage of message queue (eg: Kafka)\n-- Servers send metrics to the ingestion service, which validates and publishes them \nto a Kafka topic partitioned by metric name (or a hash of metric name + labels).\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*** High level design\n\n\n-- the most naive approach is having servers POST metrics directly to ingestion \nservice, the service do data validate and write it to store\n-- This could quickly overwhelm the service (eg: handle 5M metrics/sec)\n-- to scale this, we will introduce usage of message queue (eg: Kafka)\n-- Servers send metrics to the ingestion service, which validates and publishes them \nto a Kafka topic partitioned by metric name (or a hash of metric name + labels).\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
