    {
      "id": "-cIKb-0ZRceT79GN0lY6U",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1222.8293322691666,
      "y": 2098.344534969031,
      "width": 1058.1392822265625,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2m",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 677895816,
      "version": 85,
      "versionNonce": 1854172426,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782193951676,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-- use streaming process framework like Flink\n1. Flink reads metrics from Kafka (same topic our ingestion consumers read from)\n2. Flink maintains a windowed state (e.g., a rolling 5-minute buffer of values)\n3. Alert rules are compiled into Flink operators that continuously evaluate conditions against those windows\n4. When a threshold is violated for the configured duration, Flink emits an alert event",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-- use streaming process framework like Flink\n1. Flink reads metrics from Kafka (same topic our ingestion consumers read from)\n2. Flink maintains a windowed state (e.g., a rolling 5-minute buffer of values)\n3. Alert rules are compiled into Flink operators that continuously evaluate conditions against those windows\n4. When a threshold is violated for the configured duration, Flink emits an alert event",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "RkxIO9tRnFTUXC7Jlo5bs",
      "type": "diamond",
      "x": -694.6393173130543,
      "y": 2282.644625325615,
      "width": 843.904158813976,
      "height": 17.785598201335688,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
