      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Sx80dLl9_u0YpBk4T8LCT",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1092.7666539526115,
      "y": 2255.6074220270507,
      "width": 1319.2943115234375,
      "height": 453.36858721046383,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2p",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1087169878,
      "version": 155,
      "versionNonce": 914112650,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1782194052587,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*** How we ensure high availability of the service:\nMetrics ingestion: can we keep collecting and storing data during failures?\nAlerting and notifications: can we still detect and notify when things are breaking?\n==> The essence: never let in-flight data disappear. When things break, we degrade freshness, not correctness. \nMetrics and alerts may arrive late, but they still arrive.\n\n*** Ingestion path\n1) Agents buffer locally and retry if the network or ingestion layer is down\n2) Kafka is replicated across zones so a broker loss doesn't drop data\n3) Writes are idempotent so retries don't create duplicate points\n*** Alerting + notification path\n1) Alert evaluation state is checkpointed so a processor crash can resume\n2) Alert events are written to Kafka before any external notifications\n3) Alert Service retries delivery and can fail over to a secondary channel\n",
      "fontSize": 24.17965798455807,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*** How we ensure high availability of the service:\nMetrics ingestion: can we keep collecting and storing data during failures?\nAlerting and notifications: can we still detect and notify when things are breaking?\n==> The essence: never let in-flight data disappear. When things break, we degrade freshness, not correctness. \nMetrics and alerts may arrive late, but they still arrive.\n\n*** Ingestion path\n1) Agents buffer locally and retry if the network or ingestion layer is down\n2) Kafka is replicated across zones so a broker loss doesn't drop data\n3) Writes are idempotent so retries don't create duplicate points\n*** Alerting + notification path\n1) Alert evaluation state is checkpointed so a processor crash can resume\n2) Alert events are written to Kafka before any external notifications\n3) Alert Service retries delivery and can fail over to a secondary channel\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "sMhQ8QPPOEV6a655u-9W-",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 1047.976122669229,
